---
title: Oven-fried chicken
servings: 4
tags: [american, chicken, make-ahead]
cuisine: american
time: 1 hour 40 minutes
source: Crispy Oven-Fried Chicken by America's Test Kitchen (via AP), https://www.minotdailynews.com/life/food/2019/05/buttermilk-and-salt-key-to-this-crispy-oven-fried-chicken
---

In a #large bowl{}, whisk the @buttermilk{2%cups}, @Dijon mustard{2%tbsp},
@salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp} and @garlic powder{1%tsp}.

Pull the skin off the @chicken{3%lb}(bone-in breasts, drumsticks or thighs).
Turn them in the buttermilk, cover, and chill at least
~{30%minutes}, or overnight.

Heat the oven to 400°F with a rack in the middle. Line a #rimmed baking sheet{}
with foil, set a #wire rack{} in it, and coat the rack with
@vegetable oil{}(spray).

Crush the @cornflakes{4%cups} in a #zipper-lock bag{} with a #rolling pin{}.
Mix in the @poultry seasoning{1%tsp} and @paprika{1%tsp} and tip into a second
bowl.

Lift each piece from the buttermilk, press it into the crumbs to coat, and set
it on the rack. Spray the chicken until it looks shiny.

Bake ~{40%minutes}, until the breasts read 165°F and the legs 175°F. Cool on
the sheet ~{5%minutes} before serving.

> Start checking at 35 minutes; small pieces finish first.
